{"id": "DfIAdq3o_ae", "title": "Video by vigyan_bhairav__", "description": "The pause between two breaths 🌬️⏸️\n\nIn the Vigyan Bhairav Tantra, Bhairavi asks Shiva one question: \"How can I know you?\"\n\nHis first answer (Method 1, verse 24) is the simplest of all 112:\n\n🌬️ The out-breath (prana) rises from the heart and flows out, about twelve finger-widths beyond the nose, to a point called Dvadashanta.\n⏸️ There, for a moment, the breath stops. Nothing moves.\n🌬️ Then the in-breath (jiva) returns to the heart… and turns again. A second pause.\n\nThose two still gaps are \"the place of Shiva.\" Don't force the breath. Just notice the pause. As you keep watching, it grows longer, and in that stillness you come to know: I am Bhairava. 🔱\n\nTry it now for 5 breaths. Comment 🕉️ when you feel the gap.\n\n📖 Source: Vigyan Bhairav Tantra (Rudrayamal Tantra), Dharana 1\n🎨 Ukiyo-e woodblock-style animation\n\nFollow for one method at a time 🪷\n\n#VigyanBhairavTantra #VigyanBhairav #Bhairava #Shiva #Shakti #Tantra #KashmirShaivism #Meditation #BreathAwareness #Pranayama #Prana #Mindfulness #Stillness #SpiritualAwakening #Consciousness #Yoga #Dharana #Mahadev #HarHarMahadev #Ukiyoe #WoodblockPrint #ReelsIndia #MeditationReels #SpiritualReels", "channel": "vigyan_bhairav__", "uploader_id": "70392958166", "uploader": "Bhairav", "timestamp": 1793377623, "like_count": 14018, "comment_count": 89, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1877272603438472a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.924, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNooDr